WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.319
Westworld Season 2 Episode 2 starts with Dolores
and Arnold, thirty-five years ago.

00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:11.340
Arnold shows her a city in the real world
– possibly in China, near the Westworld

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:17.000
island . Dolores is awed with the beauty of
this place . Arnold says most people don’t

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.480
see the beauty in the world . But hosts like
Dolores, and children like Arnold’s son

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.689
Charlie, have the naivety, or the “courage”,
to see the world with all its wonders and

00:00:27.689 --> 00:00:32.680
possibilities . This is why Arnold loved the
hosts, and wanted them to be free.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.400
Though ironically, the freed hosts lose this
innocent optimism.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.010
In the present, Dolores attacks a Westworld
facility.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:45.510
She says she “used to see the beauty in
this world” but now she sees “the truth”

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:51.280
. Dolores shows Teddy his deaths and abuse
in Westworld – she opens his eyes to evil

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.190
. It’s like in the Bible, when Eve eats
the forbidden fruit, then gives a taste to

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.190
Adam.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.070
The fruit gives them knowledge of good and
evil , original sin – so they’re cast

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:07.360
out of the Garden of Eden – just like Dolores
and Teddy lose that innocence Arnold loved.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:11.460
Now that they know good and evil, Dolores
and Teddy are free to choose.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.870
Dolores choses violent vengeance – what
will Teddy do?

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.940
Back in the past, Arnold and Ford are trying
to get investment for the early Westworld

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.930
from the Delos corporation.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:27.920
So they send the hosts Angela and Akecheta
to Logan Delos, the son of company head James

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.920
Delos.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.270
So this happens before Season 1, when Logan
and William visit the park.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.600
Angela and Akecheta take Logan to a party
where everyone’s a host, to show off how

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:43.409
advanced their robot tech is – and Logan
gets a hands-on demo with Angela.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:48.840
So Logan’s convinced to invest in Westworld,
and he becomes a regular at the park.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:53.940
Then Season 1 happens – Logan’s sister
Juliet gets engaged to William , so Logan

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.840
takes William to Westworld.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.840
Will meets Dolores, then embraces his dark
side, and discredits Logan so that William

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.520
replaces Logan as James’ Delos favourite
.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:10.759
In this scene, after Season 1, William convinces
James to invest even more in Westworld.

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:16.480
He pitches the big secret Delos plan, which
is about collecting data on guest behaviour.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.660
Cause in the Westworld park, people feel free
to reveal their true desires – just like

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.870
William did in Season 1 . If Delos records
and analyses this behaviour, they could use

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:32.680
the data to predict and control peoples’
choices – like Facebook, Google and YouTube

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:33.680
do.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.300
Remember to like and subscribe.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:42.280
Later we see a retirement party for James
– William is taking over the Delos company.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.760
And there are hints of tension here.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.380
William is taking power from James.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:52.830
And James seems sick – he’s impatient
for progress on something . Does he mean some

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:53.910
medical development?

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:57.950
Do they wanna put James’ brain in a robot
body or something?

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:01.890
From the looks of the trailers, James’ story
is far from over.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:05.060
We see William’s wife Juliet, and their
daughter Emily.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:10.819
But William has also brought Dolores , which
is kinda creepy – to keep her around as

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:14.819
scenery after having falling out of love with
her last season.

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:19.440
And Will’s wife Juliet looks unhappy to
see Dolores – you gotta wonder how much

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.690
she knows about Will and Dolores’ relationship.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:27.510
We know from last season that eventually,
Juliet commits suicide because of the darkness

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.550
in William .
We see Logan moping, and doing some sci-fi

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:36.120
drugs, as you would if your father rejected
you and gave the family business to some other

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.120
guy.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:43.110
Dolores comes to Logan, possibly sent by William
to taunt Logan – as though Dolores is a

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:48.770
cruel trophy of William’s victory over Logan
. Logan says that Delos will cause “the

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:52.250
whole fucking species” to “burn” . What
does he mean?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.500
That Delos’ secret data project will hurt
humanity?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.360
That Westworld will make people dark and cruel
like William?

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.060
Or does Logan foresee the robot uprising?

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.900
He clearly knows something.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:09.060
It’ll be cool to learn more about his fate,
cause we’ve never seen Logan in the present

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.060
timeline.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.690
Is he even still alive?

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:16.949
We see William visit Dolores – who acts
passive and mute.

00:04:16.949 --> 00:04:21.569
In the park last season, William thought love
for Dolores transformed him.

00:04:21.569 --> 00:04:27.069
But now with Dolores reduced to “a thing”,
William realises it was self-discovery that

00:04:27.069 --> 00:04:32.759
changed him . In a different light, this could
be a positive message – to self-actualise,

00:04:32.759 --> 00:04:35.449
without defining yourself by others.

00:04:35.449 --> 00:04:40.460
But unfortunately, the self William discovers
is a sociopathic asshat.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.840
And he has plans.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:48.349
William shows Dolores some kind of construction
project, connected to the data collection

00:04:48.349 --> 00:04:49.349
plan.

00:04:49.349 --> 00:04:54.240
He says it’s “an answer” to “a question
no one's ever even dreamed of asking” . And

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.340
this place becomes the big mystery of this
episode.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:03.949
Cause now, thirty-five years later, both William
and Dolores are trying to return to this place.

00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:08.719
Old William – the Man in Black – rescues
the host Lawrence from some other hosts, “the

00:05:08.719 --> 00:05:09.979
Pardue brothers”.

00:05:09.979 --> 00:05:14.809
Will says that in this narrative loop, Lawrence
is meant to escape the brothers himself . But

00:05:14.809 --> 00:05:18.509
since all the hosts have gone rogue, they’re
acting differently.

00:05:18.509 --> 00:05:23.499
One brother gets up and keeps fighting after
William shoots him dead . So the rules of

00:05:23.499 --> 00:05:27.439
the Westworld game have changed . The difficulty
has increased.

00:05:27.439 --> 00:05:33.490
The enemies have more HP, and it’s ironman
Nuzlocke mode – you can die for real.

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:38.619
So William has to use all his knowledge of
the game to survive – he goes to a bar,

00:05:38.619 --> 00:05:43.779
and grabs a high tech health pack from a wall
– like that chicken in Castlevania.

00:05:43.779 --> 00:05:47.110
William is determined to beat this end-game
quest.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:51.180
But then he says that Westworld “is goin'
down in flames”, and everyone’s gonna

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.550
die , but it’s not clear why.

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.460
Does he think Dolores’ war will kill them
all?

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:00.469
Or does this connect to what Logan said about
the species burning?

00:06:00.469 --> 00:06:04.819
Whatever the reason, William’s excited by
this apocalypse – says it’s “a chance

00:06:04.819 --> 00:06:10.059
to see what we're really made of, a glimpse
of the men we could've been” . It’s a

00:06:10.059 --> 00:06:16.490
sad dumb tragedy that William has spent decades
so obsessed with discovering his true self,

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:21.369
that he never got around to living his life
– being himself – so all that’s left

00:06:21.369 --> 00:06:25.059
for him now is “a glimpse” of what he
“could've been”.

00:06:25.059 --> 00:06:29.729
William’s a man defined by his past and
regrets.

00:06:29.729 --> 00:06:35.279
William says Delos has been watching, “tallying
up” peoples’ sins in the park – he must

00:06:35.279 --> 00:06:39.899
mean the guest data project that he himself
started.

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:44.531
William says he “built” “this place”,
and it’s his “greatest mistake” . He

00:06:44.531 --> 00:06:49.770
says he’s been judged for his sins in the
park – and he does have many sins.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:54.509
But he thinks judgement is unfair – cause
why should he be judged for hurting robots,

00:06:54.509 --> 00:06:57.129
when the robots were meant to be mindless
machines?

00:06:57.129 --> 00:06:58.910
The stakes weren’t real.

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:03.210
So William wants to “appeal the verdict”,
clear his name, then “burn” the whole

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:09.870
thing “to the ground” . So if this mysterious
place is where the Westworld data is stored,

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:13.620
maybe William wants to wipe his files to avoid
judgement.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:20.439
But with all the talk of burning and God and
“a question”, there must be deeper meaning

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:21.819
here.

00:07:21.819 --> 00:07:25.779
William and Lawrence head to Pariah, and meet
El Lazo.

00:07:25.779 --> 00:07:31.439
As William points out, El Lazo was a role
played by Lawrence back in the Season 1 timeline.

00:07:31.439 --> 00:07:36.159
Lazo talks about his revolution storyline
– says now that he’s reached its end,

00:07:36.159 --> 00:07:41.919
he sees it was empty all along – just like
Hector with that safe . The freed hosts are

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:47.360
realising that their lives are lies, scripts
written to entertain guests.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:50.120
So what do they do with themselves now?

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.990
William could face the same problem.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:56.649
What if he reaches the end of his “find
the door” quest, and just feels empty – what

00:07:56.649 --> 00:07:57.649
next?

00:07:57.649 --> 00:08:03.249
Lazo finds no joy in quests, so he refuses
to help William with his journey .

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:08.240
And Lazo tells a story about how elephants
can be trained to stay in place with just

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:13.469
a stake – if the elephant learns from a
young age it’s too weak to escape, it won’t

00:08:13.469 --> 00:08:18.050
even try when it’s older and stronger . The
lesson is that sometimes we’re held back

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:24.029
not by the realities of our situation, but
by our beliefs and our fears and our past.

00:08:24.029 --> 00:08:29.419
Maybe for William to truly escape Westworld,
he needs to let go of his past with Dolores,

00:08:29.419 --> 00:08:35.310
Logan, Delos – Robert says last episode
that William’s quest “ends where [he]

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:38.470
began” .
William tries to recruit Lazo’s men, but

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:42.780
Ford’s programming kicks in, and the hosts
all kill themselves, so that William can’t

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:43.780
use them.

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:49.160
Even after his death, Ford is manipulating
William . Which raises the question of just

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:53.710
how much control Ford has over the broader
storyline of this place of judgement.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:59.140
Dolores, meanwhile, chokes a bloke in robot
yoghurt, to make him tell her Delos’ security

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.140
plan.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:04.240
Apparently, they’ll rally hundreds of men
, which is prolly what we saw on the beach

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.710
last episode.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:12.240
Dolores only has like fifty hosts, so she
needs allies to win this war . She meets Maeve,

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:17.000
and tries to recruit her to the robot revenge
army , but Maeve’s not interested.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.830
She points out the hypocrisy of how Dolores
commands people when she says she’s fighting

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:28.210
for freedom . Maeve pointedly asks Teddy if
he feels free . Maybe after getting woke this

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:33.070
episode, Teddy will finally start making his
own decisions on what’s right.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:38.380
Dolores then meets with Confederado soldiers
– who are cosplaying as the Last Supper.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:43.260
Apparently they’re headed for Glory , aka
“The Valley Beyond”, which seems to be

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.890
that same place that William’s headed.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:51.350
If the Confederados are the apostles of the
Last Supper, Dolores is the Jesus.

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:55.520
Cause when the soldiers threaten Dolores,
she says to forgive them cause they “don’t

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:00.870
know any better” which is totally a Jesus
catchphrase . Dolores then murders them all,

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:06.760
which is less Jesus-y, but then she uses her
Westworld tech to resurrect their leader Craddock,

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.370
like how Jesus resurrects Lazarus.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:15.300
Dolores then claims to have killed God , which
is true in the sense that she killed Westworld’s

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.720
creator, Ford.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:21.280
Dolores tells Craddock he’ll need her favour
to reach Glory.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:24.360
So there are heavy religious themes here.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:30.270
Dolores frames herself as a messianic figure,
but also claims to have killed God, so maybe

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:35.090
she’s more like Satan – a fallen angel
who rebels against God .

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:41.090
Dolores marches on with her Confederado army,
including the resurrected Craddock.

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:46.830
There is something about leading an army of
undead Confederate soldiers that gives off…

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.800
kind of a bad guy vibe?

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:52.970
Not to mention Dolores’ torture and murder
of innocents.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:57.590
She does have a bit of a breaker of chains
Daenerys feel sometimes, but she can also

00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:03.100
seem a bit like the Night King – what with
the exterminating humans thing.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.320
Is Dolores a hero, or a villain?

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.910
Dolores talks with Teddy about “Glory”.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:13.750
He says that Glory and “The Valley Beyond”
are all names for the same place . Dolores

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:18.250
equates it with William’s place of judgement,
the Delos data project.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:23.110
She says she knows what’s there because
William showed her , she was present at his

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:24.960
pitch thirty years ago.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:30.440
Dolores says this place is a weapon and she’ll
use it to “destroy them” . If Glory is

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:35.170
the place where guest behaviour data is stored,
maybe Dolores plans to release the data to

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:39.030
show the world all the awful things that Westworld
guests have done.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:43.530
It’d be like in South Park when everyone’s
internet history’s made public – it could

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.340
cause chaos.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:48.180
But the weapon seems bigger than that.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:54.200
It’s tied to ideas of judgement, fire, God,
“an answer” to “a question no one's

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:56.240
ever even dreamed of asking”.

00:11:56.240 --> 00:12:00.350
And the flooded valley with drowned hosts
last episode.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:05.570
This is shaping up to be the central mystery
of the season, and it’s kinda hard to imagine

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:08.230
a payoff that justifies this hype.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:13.930
Like, the maze was the centre of last season,
and it paid off in only very vague ways.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:17.070
So maybe we shouldn’t expect hard answers
here.

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:22.480
But this episode does make sense, in a way
that most of last season didn’t.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:26.791
Back then, we didn’t know characters’
motivations, which people were robots, or

00:12:26.791 --> 00:12:28.980
even which timeline was which.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.750
But this episode’s pretty clear.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:35.500
We get the backstory of Arnold and Logan and
Delos, while in the present Dolores fights

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.330
her war against humans.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:38.960
Maeve tries to find her daughter.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.000
And William pursues his quest.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:45.380
We know who people are, and what they want,
which gives the show space to explore some

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:50.180
cool themes – from the Bible, to modern
technology, to elephants.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:54.180
So let us know in the comments what you think
of this new Westworld.

